analysis:
Examined the ProviderLoop+StartupPreload.swift base/head diff and the ProviderLoop.swift state-declaration patch.

StartupPreload changes:
- canLoadMore now calls startupPreloadCanLoadMore (head 313-315). It adds a watchdog stop flag (startupPreloadStopRequested) to the existing slot-cap check.
- markStartupPreloadReached stamps startupPreloadCandidate and calls transitionGenerations.begin (head 321-322).
- finishStartupPreload resets both new fields (head 306-307).

These changes can only stop preloading earlier, before the next candidate. They do not alter:
- the fail-closed self-test retirement (failedSelfTestHashes, unadvertise, reconnect; head 393-448);
- the advertised-set filter;
- the allowEviction:false load;
- the registration gate.

A watchdog stop leaves models cold, which falls back to the lazy-load path. That is an availability tradeoff, not a trust bypass. One case was considered: a stop landing mid-self-test. The current step is documented as never interrupted, so retirement still completes.

ProviderLoop.swift adds in-memory state declarations only:
- named autopilotHistory tuple with a detail field;
- autopilot adopted IDs and holds;
- download settings override, storage report and download coordinator;
- inventory-awaiting-registration set and candidate verification task;
- test seam;
- busy clock, transition watchdog and stalled command ID;
- preload stop/candidate fields, reslice generation and transition generations.

The behavior behind these declarations lives in files not supplied here. These include ProviderLoop+AutopilotPlacement, ProviderLoop+AutopilotDownload and superviseTransitions. Integration should verify the following:
(1) Autopilot download-coordinator builds are hash-verified before joining inventory, and are not advertised until registration (T-012, T-027, T-054).
2. autopilotRegistrationSeamForTesting is nil and unreachable in production builds.
3. Watchdog cancellation (autopilotStalledCommandId) cannot leave a partially loaded or unverified model advertised, or leave stale capacity (T-029).
4. The autopilotHistory detail strings are not exposing sensitive paths or consumer data through status reporting (T-058).

No concrete regression is visible in the supplied lines.
